<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bloody Christmas (1920)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bloody Christmas was the Italian army and navy attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rijeka">Fiume</a>, now Rijeka, from 24 to 29 December 1920, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabriele-dannunzio">Gabriele D'Annunzio</a>'s occupation of the city. After the Treaty of Rapallo made Fiume a free state, D'Annunzio refused to leave, and Italian forces under General Enrico Caviglia shelled and stormed the city. Several dozen people were killed before D'Annunzio surrendered.</p></div>
